cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Real-Space, Regularization-Invariant Metric for
  Density-Functional Error: reference implementation
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software
  (this file) and the accompanying article (preferred-citation).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Juan Carlos
    family-names: Alatorre-Martinez
    email: jcarlosam1999@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Tonalá, Jalisco, Mexico"
  - given-names: Miriam Guadalupe
    family-names: Rafael-Cano
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Tonalá, Jalisco, Mexico"
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jcarlosam1999/MAPA-metric'
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a real-space, regularization-invariant
  metric for auditing density-functional error, built on the Wu-Yang
  inversion of the Kohn-Sham potential applied to multi-reference
  densities along dissociation coordinates. A single entry point
  reproduces every result of the accompanying article for ten
  fundamental diatomic systems: the reference densities, their
  inversion, the potential and response metrics in exact and
  self-consistent density modes, the density-reproduction confidence
  gate, and the validations reported in the Supporting Information.
keywords:
  - density functional theory
  - Kohn-Sham inversion
  - exchange-correlation potential
  - static correlation
  - self-interaction error
  - regularization
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-08'
